                        android:text="Standard First Aid Rule: Automated External Defibrillators (AEDs) are not routinely used on neonates (newborns under 1 month old) in basic beginner first aid.\n\nYour Task: Do not look for or wait for an AED. Focus entirely on maintaining the flawless, continuous 3:1 compression-to-breath loop to keep their brain oxygenated until paramedics arrive with specialized neonatal equipment."
